ack to the physical resolver after routes apply. 4. The accountable product and architecture owner records approval, or the task remains blocked with the exact choice and evidence still required. 5. Downstream DNS implementation, M4 profile UI, M2 relay, documentation, and validation tasks are listed by concrete ID and impact.","assignee":"","blockedBy":[],"blocks":["TASK-260715-2pml0c","TASK-260715-5o6jqg","TASK-260715-1o4h97"],"checklist":[{"text":"Compare all viable resolver policies against privacy bootstrap UX and reliability criteria","done":false},{"text":"Obtain an accountable decision with exact schema defaults and failure semantics","done":false},{"text":"Attach task-scoped decision record and downstream impact list","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:17:04Z","description":"Resolve the product and architecture gap that the baseline profile fields do not identify which resolver M1 should reach through SSH. Compare explicit per-profile resolver endpoints, a documented product default, exit-host discovery, and tunneled DoH where relevant, then record one implementable privacy-safe policy and migration path.","id":"TASK-260715-1tnjlu","isBlocked":false,"name":"decide-baseline-exit-dns-resolver-policy","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-2bfjhn","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: IPv4 and IPv6 resolver addresses, port and protocol, profile-schema impact, default behavior, reachability from the exit host, bootstrap circularity, DNSSEC transparency, TCP support, privacy and operator expectations, failure behavior, M4 UI impact, test fixtures, and future M2 relay compatibility. Out of scope: implementing DNS, selecting a public vendor without accountable approval, silently using the physical resolver, remote shell parsing without a security design, fake DNS, and final UI copy.","status":"backlog","title":"Decide the baseline exit-side DNS resolver policy","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:28:50Z"},{"ac":"1. Golden cases produce both default families, exact host exclusions, tunnel-owned DNS, and accepted MTU with no unrelated or broad excluded route. 2. Invalid or conflicting addresses, wrong endpoint family, broad prefixes, missing DNS, unsupported MTU, stale endpoint evidence, and settings callback failure are rejected or rolled back deterministically. 3. Instrumented adapter tests prove SSH actual endpoint capture precedes settings and settings success precedes packet reads and usable capability. 4. Separate iOS and macOS cases record whether Apple automatic tunnel-server exclusion is relied on, supplemented, or rejected according to the approved contract. 5. Tests use only public Network Extension and Darwin abstractions and privacy-safe summaries and fail on private utun discovery or full-address logging.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-2tj2pb","TASK-260715-12tbjl","TASK-260715-30ugfm"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-336ljl","TASK-260715-1o4h97"],"checklist":[{"text":"Cover dual-stack settings collisions exact exclusions ordering and rollback","done":false},{"text":"Run iOS and macOS platform-branch and public-API regression tests","done":false},{"text":"Attach task-scoped golden summaries and results","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:17:04Z","description":"Build pure settings and provider-adapter tests for virtual address collision handling, IPv4 and IPv6 default routes, actual SSH endpoint host exclusions, DNS ownership, MTU, Apple automatic tunnel-server behavior instrumentation, ordering, and rollback on both supported platforms.","id":"TASK-260715-293sz3","isBlocked":true,"name":"add-route-and-endpoint-exclusion-tests","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-2bfjhn","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: settings value golden tests, v4 and v6 endpoints, candidate versus actual endpoint changes, host prefix lengths, no broad exclusions, virtual address collisions, absent family, accepted M0 MTU, tunnel DNS and match domains, platform capability branches, application callback success or failure, packet-read ordering, and diagnostics summaries. Out of scope: live path migration, NAT64 transition, captive portals, fail-closed mode, physical leak capture owned separately, reconnect, general UDP, and private Apple APIs.","status":"backlog","title":"Add dual-stack route and SSH endpoint exclusion tests","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:28:50Z"},{"ac":"1. Cache entries and total bytes have fixed configurable ceilings, use injected time, expire by protocol TTL policy, and are cleared on profile or resolver identity change. 2. Positive and negative responses cache only when semantically permitted, negative TTL follows authoritative data bounds, and malformed, truncated, transient-failure, or policy-excluded responses do not poison the cache. 3. Client UDP responses respect the advertised or baseline size and set TC when required so the client can retry TCP, while TCP clients receive the complete permitted response. 4. Concurrent identical misses coalesce without cross-client ID corruption, and cancellation or upstream failure returns a bounded explicit failure with no physical query. 5. Deterministic tests cover TTL boundaries, negative caching, eviction, size pressure, TC retry, mixed UDP and TCP clients, resolver change, malformed data, and query-name-free metrics.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-1e0x1u","TASK-260715-5o6jqg"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-393tuu","TASK-260715-30ugfm"],"checklist":[{"text":"Implement protocol-correct bounded cache and client truncation behavior","done":false},{"text":"Run fake-clock TTL negative eviction coalescing and TC tests","done":false},{"text":"Attach task-scoped cache policy and verification evidence","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:17:04Z","description":"Implement the DNS transaction policy around listener and tunneled upstream: bounded positive and negative caching, TTL expiry, request coalescing where safe, client