[{"ac":"1. Host-key policy runs before any user-authentication request and no bypass or accept-all mode exists in production composition. 2. First use returns full algorithm and SHA-256 fingerprint evidence plus canonical host for an explicit containing-app trust action and does not authenticate. 3. An approved fingerprint connects, while a changed, revoked, unsupported, or host-mismatched key fails without automatic retry or opening destination channels. 4. Rotation with multiple approved keys has deterministic precedence and records only non-secret provenance and timestamps. 5. Tests include same key, different key, same bytes with invalid algorithm label, malformed key, multiple approvals, revocation, canonical-host mismatch, and logging redaction.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-29ws8l"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-3t2v9w","TASK-260715-3cv3r4"],"checklist":[{"text":"Implement pre-authentication host policy with no production bypass","done":false},{"text":"Run first-use match change rotation revocation and redaction tests","done":false},{"text":"Attach task-scoped policy and ordering evidence","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:16:33Z","description":"Implement the candidate-neutral host-key policy invoked by the selected SSH adapter before user authentication acceptance. Compare raw server key evidence with the approved profile identities, return explicit trust-required evidence on first use, reject change or revocation, and preserve privacy-safe audit metadata.","id":"TASK-260715-12zaq5","isBlocked":true,"name":"implement-approved-host-identity-policy","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-2wjwuf","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: SSH key algorithm normalization, SHA-256 fingerprint calculation and constant-time comparison where appropriate, multiple approved keys for rotation, provenance and first or last seen updates through a non-secret result, first-use evidence, changed key, unsupported algorithm, revoked