ailure at every startup step rolls back exactly the resources already acquired in reverse order and completes once. 5. At stop, all reads, tasks, timers, channels, native runtimes, sockets, and retained configuration references return to the recorded baseline.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-lovbdz","TASK-260715-3ejhyy"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-32virr","TASK-260715-30ugfm","TASK-260715-1bp6eu","TASK-260715-2hiabd","TASK-260715-3dv8ea"],"checklist":[{"text":"Implement the approved state machine with generation-safe structured cancellation","done":false},{"text":"Verify every partial-start rollback and repeated stop path","done":false},{"text":"Attach task-scoped lifecycle and resource-cleanup evidence","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:16:07Z","description":"Implement the shared asynchronous coordinator that owns one M1 tunnel generation from validated configuration through authenticated SSH, prepared packet and DNS components, route application, packet reads, usable-state publication, failure rollback, and deterministic stop.","id":"TASK-260715-3tlgwm","isBlocked":true,"name":"implement-tunnel-runtime-coordinator","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-1y04r0","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: state machine from disconnected through starting, usable TCP and DNS, stopping, and failed, generation tokens, structured cancellation, serialized transitions, dependency health callbacks, ordered rollback, idempotent stop, and future capability hooks. Out of scope: NETunnelProviderManager, profile UI, detailed SSH policy, TCP or DNS internals, UDP, multi-lane scheduling, reasserting reconnect behavior, memory-watermark tuning, and final UI state wording.","status":"backlog","title":"Implement the extension-owned M1 TunnelRuntimeCoordinator","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:29:21Z"},{"ac":"1. Every message has a documented version, maximum encoded size, required fields, defaults, and stable error for unsupported input. 2. Configuration contains only non-secret identifiers and opaque references, with tests proving private-key and passphrase bytes cannot be represented. 3. Capability snapshots independently represent TCP, safe DNS, UDP, route mode, and runtime health without falsely claiming M2 full mode. 4. Round-trip, unknown-field, corrupt-payload, oversize, and old or future version tests are deterministic. 5. The models compile for ReluxTunnelCore, both hosts, and both providers without platform-specific transport types leaking into shared code.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-30zng6"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-3tlgwm","TASK-260715-1i49fm","TASK-260715-3f4lxy","TASK-260715-15vkvz","TASK-260715-1rsqrh","TASK-260715-1bp6eu"],"checklist":[{"text":"Implement every versioned model and bound defined by the approved runtime contract","done":false},{"text":"Run codec compatibility security and size-bound tests on all shared targets","done":false},{"text":"Attach task-scoped implementation and verification evidence","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:16:07Z","description":"Implement candidate-neutral shared Swift models and codecs for the non-secret provider configuration reference, start request, commands, capability snapshot, lifecycle snapshot, diagnostics snapshot, and protocol errors defined by the runtime contract.","id":"TASK-260715-lovbdz","isBlocked":true,"name":"implement-versioned-runtime-contract-models","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-1y04r0","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: explicit schema versions, Codable or equivalent deterministic encoding, size bounds, unknown-field tolerance, unsupported-version rejection, opaque profile and Keychain reference identifiers, capability booleans, lifecycle state, redacted errors, and unit-test fixtures. Out of scope: raw secrets, profile editing, NETunnelProviderManager persistence, transport implementation, UI rendering, and compatibility with undocumented legacy payloads.","status":"backlog","title":"Implement versioned runtime configuration and message models","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:29:21Z"},{"ac":"1. A harness command starts the composed runtime from a fixture profile, observes the ordered states, exchanges representative TCP and DNS fixture traffic, requests diagnostics, and stops cleanly. 2. Separate scenarios inject authentication, packet, DNS, route-apply, and mid-session mandatory failures with stable expected exit codes. 3. The harness verifies no live forwarding dependency on a simulated host-app lifetime after start. 4. Repeated runs report zero monotonic descriptor, task, channel, socket, or native-runtime growth. 5. Fixture versions, dependency revisions, commands, expected outputs, and privacy-safe logs are documented and runnable in CI.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-32virr","TASK-260715-3ejhyy"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-2rcvr0","TASK-260715-1gvdtz","TASK-260715-336ljl"],"checklist":[{"text":"Add successful and mandatory-failure composed runtime scenarios","done":false},{"text":"Run repeated harness scenarios with resource and privacy assertions","done":false},{"text":"Attach task-scoped fixture manifest commands and results","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:16:07Z","description":"Extend the M0 harness with black-box scenarios that construct the production shared factories against controlled packet, SSH, TCP, DNS, and route substitutes and drive one complete M1 runtime generation without a containing app or Network Extension process.","id":"TASK-260715-m8bi8i","isBlocked":true,"name":"add-shared-runtime-harness-integration-tests","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-1y04r0","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: versioned configuration input, selected dependency composition, successful startup and traffic-ready snapshot, injected SSH or DNS loss, stop, repeated generations, aggregate diagnostics, fixture manifests, and CI-suitable deterministic e