mains, platform capability branches, application callback success or failure, packet-read ordering, and diagnostics summaries. Out of scope: live path migration, NAT64 transition, captive portals, fail-closed mode, physical leak capture owned separately, reconnect, general UDP, and private Apple APIs.","status":"backlog","title":"Add dual-stack route and SSH endpoint exclusion tests","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:28:50Z"},{"ac":"1. Cache entries and total bytes have fixed configurable ceilings, use injected time, expire by protocol TTL policy, and are cleared on profile or resolver identity change. 2. Positive and negative responses cache only when semantically permitted, negative TTL follows authoritative data bounds, and malformed, truncated, transient-failure, or policy-excluded responses do not poison the cache. 3. Client UDP responses respect the advertised or baseline size and set TC when required so the client can retry TCP, while TCP clients receive the complete permitted response. 4. Concurrent identical misses coalesce without cross-client ID corruption, and cancellation or upstream failure returns a bounded explicit failure with no physical query. 5. Deterministic tests cover TTL boundaries, negative caching, eviction, size pressure, TC retry, mixed UDP and TCP clients, resolver change, malformed data, and query-name-free metrics.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-1e0x1u","TASK-260715-5o6jqg"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-393tuu","TASK-260715-30ugfm"],"checklist":[{"text":"Implement protocol-correct bounded cache and client truncation behavior","done":false},{"text":"Run fake-clock TTL negative eviction coalescing and TC tests","done":false},{"text":"Attach task-scoped cache policy and verification evidence","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:17:04Z","description":"Implement the DNS transaction policy around listener and tunneled upstream: bounded positive and negative caching, TTL expiry, request coalescing where safe, client